1 EXIT

   Ends the command procedure (or CALL subroutine) it is in; the command
   level that ran it goes on.

   Format

     EXIT [status]

2 Parameter

 status

   An expression (see Symbol_Assign Expressions) whose integer value is
   the procedure's status, the $STATUS of the level that ran it.  A
   status that isn't a success (an even number) has its message shown
   there, unless its bit 28 says it has been shown already.  Without a
   status, the procedure's status is $STATUS, marked as shown.  See
   Symbol_Assign Status.

2 Description

   At the terminal (command level 0), EXIT ends govax.  In
   a subprocess's DCL, EXIT at command level 0 logs the subprocess out,
   as LOGOUT does.

2 Examples

   1.$ EXIT 1

     Ends the procedure successfully.

   2.$ EXIT %X10000002

     Ends the procedure with an error whose message isn't shown.
